it's no surprise the crab accidentally  became an instagram sensation when the  public was able to see this huge  creature flailing in the wind and  honestly looking a little bit ridiculous  that was amazing the crew had their fair  share of laughs over the crab's presence  as well  especially when it was time to deflate  not an  easy task let's just say it involved a  lot of  rolling around and stomping in attempts  to expel all the air  oh yeah when the crab uses its claw  believe it or not  that's almost entirely practical effects  the team had rented a fairly inexpensive  excavator  yes like a construction site excavator  and  souped it right up they took off the  bucket that would normally be at the end  of the arm and attached a claw instead  the whole thing was dressed in blue to  incorporate cgi after the fact  this is probably the first time we've  ever heard of a prop character having a  sort of body double  okay  considering how massive and intricate  some of the creatures were it was really  surprising to learn just how much was  actually results of practical effects  and builds  not just for us though for the creators  too the effects specialists feel that  all the practical effects were a big  contributor to actually grounding the  film  the super cool robot mavis was what the  creators expected to be the most  challenging build  but apart from a couple of small details  the mavis we see on screen was the  practical  puppet built mavis may not have been a  real robot  but it was made out of many pieces a bit  over a hundred parts made with a 3d  printer actually  getting all those parts together now  that was a stressful challenge  only four hours before they shot with  mavis the crew was staring at  all the pieces sitting apart but as we  can see  it all worked out mavis's faceplate and  a bit of the left hand had some cgi work  done  but the biggest change really was hiding  the puppet master who was behind mavis  dressed in a full gray suit  how about that bug monster well it was  an impressive 80  practical piece with digital legs added  to it afterwards  this kind of creature is actually what  inspired the special effects artist  stephen boyle to pursue a career in  effects  the creation was definitely his favorite  of all in this movie  he really appreciated the creativity he  got to put into it  all those creepy crawly way too big for  comfort  sand gobblers acting as kind of  underground tremors were a mix of  puppets ranging from 40 feet to a meter  long and cgi  the queen gobbler that exploded was a  full build for the team  this bulbous and slimy giant frog  creation  well sections of it were built but the  whole of the monster itself was created  digitally  considering how much was practically  created the budget for those was still  smaller than the special effects budget  they definitely matched up in terms of  quality though  the surprisingly friendly boulder snail  about a 15 foot tall and 15 to 20 foot  wide in diameter cgi creation  with every detail covered down to the  slime that coats it  then we get into the stuff of nightmares  as if we weren't there already  yes we're talking about the sirens the  kind of oversized  centipede looking monster for a  relatively blind creature those large  antennae do an  excellent job at helping it navigate  around and totally terrify us  when the film was in post-production it  was realized that the scale of the siren  had to be made even bigger than what  they'd shot for  so vfx was able to scale the creature up  and honestly  it looks pretty flawless  we all know dylan o'brien is an amazing  actor from his performances in the maze  runner movies  but what exactly were his imaginary  co-stars like  well sometimes he was acting terrified  or battling with large blue poles with  some orange on them as we can see here  to mark the size and location of his  acting partner  though luckily not all his co-stars were  imaginary  nor were they human yes we're talking  about hero and dodge  aka the dog named boy o'brien grew  extremely close with his canine co-stars  who did  totally steal the show the animal  coordinator actually said that she'd  never seen such a strong bond between an  actor and these dogs on a set before  it is probably the strongest real life  off-camera bond that we've had with one  of our animals  hero and dodge are very friendly  normally but they put on their best  performances in the scenes where they  appear to be rougher and more aggressive  they were such pros that most of the  shots the teams needed from the dogs  were captured in only one or two takes  o'brien shared in an interview that  working with the dogs and animal  coordinators was definitely one of the  highlights for him  and he hoped to be able to go and visit  them again someday this is a dog  he's brilliant he also noted that they  were excellent cuddle buddies between  takes  we'd probably do the same if we were in  his position maybe all the snuggling  time is the reason he never actually  practiced  drawing we hate to disappoint but all  the beautiful pictures we see later in  the movie  those were actually created by a member  of the props team since in actuality  o'brien is not the best artist early on  in the process he actually did do his  own  drawing which he hoped could be used as  the first example that we see of his  drawing that isn't supposed to look very  good anyway but  even that effort didn't make the cut i  freaking love it that's super sweet  because it's terrible in terms of the  world we're immersed in through the film  the monsters definitely play a major  part but so too does the environment  itself  while the film is meant to take place in  california it was shot in this very  special location in australia chosen  because it already looked so  magical and mystical as it was really  emanating the feeling they wanted the  world of the movie to have  the crew even commented on how magical  the sun looked down under  that alone added to the gorgeous world  we see the team described the area as  looking naturally futuristic  otherworldly and as if all the creatures  they created could  actually be found there there is no  place for mankind on land  the beach area we see here was  completely created in a cove that's  normally covered in grass and park  benches  but it's totally unrecognizable after  the transformation  so how did they do it 600 tons of sand  to restore the whole cove to how it  looked before took about three full  weeks  at least they were working in a  beautiful place with that golden  australia sun though  beautiful it's just not safe right it's  pretty incredible to see how creative  the teams behind the magic are  who knew so many of these complex  creations were created practically  and on such a low budget combined with  dylan o'brien and of course  the real star boy the dog it makes for  an  amazing film were you as blown away by  the mavis puppet as we were
 

